      "service": null,
      "publicDescription": "If you reuse an `Options` instance and pass `Properties` to `DefaultParser.parse()`, the first parse leaves the property value behind in the `Option` registered in `Options`: `handleProperties()` called `processValue()` on that registered option rather than on the copy that goes into the `CommandLine`, and nothing ever clears it. From then on the same `Options` gives wrong answers:\n\nThe fix adds the value to the copy instead, the same way values from the command line are handled, so parsing no longer changes the values of the registered options. A value the option already has still wins over the property, as `testPropertiesPreserveExistingOptionValue()` expects, and the `parse(Options, Properties, NonOptionAction, String...)` Javadoc now says so. The three new tests in `DefaultParserTest` fail on master and pass with the change.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with Claude Code",
      "packetSha256": "aa7966234d54b48bdd7e38259bddb8d4b572152513b9ea18fa257f75d9e3ef0b"
    },
